A packaged app (an MSIX package, such as PowerShell from the Microsoft Store) whose start carries
PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_JOB_LIST (0004) fails with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED when another process of its package runs:
Windows then cannot add the new process to the package's Desktop AppX container. ngterm-pty starts such a child
suspended instead, assigns it to its job and resumes it, which needs the main thread handle that CreateProcessW gives
and portable-pty closes. `ConPtyMasterPty::spawn_command_suspended` starts the child with CREATE_SUSPENDED and no job
list, and returns that thread handle with the child. ngterm's own. Remove when portable-pty can start a child
suspended. Its test: ngterm-pty's `a_store_powershell_pane_starts_and_its_tree_ends_with_it` (a Windows machine with
that PowerShell) and, on CI, `a_child_started_suspended_prints_to_its_console`.

